## CVE-2020-8608 vs CVE-2019-6788 — Same Bug, Different QEMU Version

Both CVEs are in `slirp/tcp_subr.c:tcp_emu()`:
- CVE-2019-6788: QEMU 3.1.0, IRC DCC SEND rewrite (`snprintf(bptr, m->m_size, ...)`)
- CVE-2020-8608: QEMU 4.2.1, same pattern, more paths exploitable

The root fix for both: use `M_FREEROOM(m)` (= available space from current `m_data`)
instead of `m->m_size` as the snprintf limit.

```c
// Fix:
m->m_len += snprintf(bptr, M_FREEROOM(m) - (bptr - m->m_data), "DCC SEND ...", ...);
// Where: M_FREEROOM(m) = m->m_size - M_ROOM(m) and M_ROOM(m) = m->m_data - m->m_dat
```

