## SLiRP CVE Trigger: EMU_FTP vs EMU_IRC

| Protocol | Port  | Trigger                          | Overflow vector             |
|----------|-------|----------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| FTP      | 21    | `PORT h1,h2,h3,h4,p1,p2` command| snprintf with `m_size-m_len`|
| IRC      | 6667  | `DCC SEND name ip port size`     | snprintf with `m_size` only |
| TFTP     | 69    | large TFTP DATA packet           | memcpy beyond mbuf end      |

EMU_IRC is triggered by `so_lport == 6667` (GUEST SOURCE port, not destination).
Always bind() source port to 6667 before connect() in guest exploit code.

EMU_FTP overflow: `snprintf(bptr, m_size - m_len, ...)` — the limit is `H_OFFSET`
bytes larger than the actual available space from bptr, giving up to 88 bytes of overflow.
However, the FTP PORT string is only ~25 bytes, so the overflow is small in practice.

