## Building Notes

- All CVE exploits: `gcc -static -O0 -g -o exp exp.c && ./pack.sh`
- `static` is essential: guest kernel has no shared libraries mounted
- `-O0`: disables optimizations that might reorder or eliminate the exploit primitives
- `pack.sh` regenerates `rootfs.cpio` from the `rootfs/` directory

CVE-2015-3456 (VENOM) / CVE-2016-4952: need `--python=python2` and QEMU 2.x quirks.
CVE-2019-6788 / CVE-2019-14378 / CVE-2020-8608: QEMU 3.x–4.x, glibc standard build.
Scavenger (CVE-2020-25084): needs `--extra-cflags="-pg"` + nm symbol offsets in exp.c.
